.TH PROX2 1 "2026-10-12" "prox2 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
prox2 \- inspect and configure a Logitech PRO X Superlight 2 mouse
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B prox2
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B prox2
talks to the mouse through the Lightspeed receiver (046d:c54d) using the hidraw interface.
It shows the mouse state, battery and profiles, changes the report rate and the DPI,
saves and restores the profile sectors, and opens a local web panel.
.PP
Access to the receiver needs the udev rule installed by the package.
Plug the receiver again after installing it.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show name, firmware, mode, active profile, current report rate and DPI,
and the state of each profile sector.
.TP
.B bateria " [\-\-seguir]"
Show the battery level. With
.BR \-\-seguir ,
keep printing battery, connection and receiver events until Ctrl+C.
.TP
.BR rate " " \fIhz\fR " [\-\-perfil " \fIN\fR " ...]"
Set the report rate. Valid values for
.I hz
are 125, 250, 500, 1000, 2000, 4000 and 8000, limited to the rates the mouse supports.
.TP
.BR dpi " " \fIn\fR " [\-\-perfil " \fIN\fR " ...]"
Set the DPI of the profiles. Valid values are 100 to 200 in steps of 1,
200 to 500 in steps of 2, 500 to 1000 in steps of 5, 1000 to 2000 in steps of 10,
2000 to 5000 in steps of 20, 5000 to 10000 in steps of 50,
10000 to 20000 in steps of 100, 20000 to 32000 in steps of 125
and 32000 to 44000 in steps of 200.
An invalid value stops with an error that lists the nearest valid ones.
.TP
.BI backup " file"
Save the profile sectors to
.I file
(JSON).
.TP
.BR restaurar " " \fIfile\fR " [\-\-sim]"
Write the sectors saved in
.I file
back to the mouse. It asks for confirmation unless
.B \-\-sim
is given. Sectors with an invalid CRC in the file are skipped.
.TP
.B painel " [\-\-porta " \fIport\fR "] [\-\-sem\-navegador]"
Open the local web panel. With
.B \-\-porta
use a fixed local port (default 0, any free port).
With
.B \-\-sem\-navegador
do not open the browser. The panel closes by itself 120 seconds after the page is closed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-perfil " " \fIN\fR " ..."
For
.B rate
and
.BR dpi :
profile sectors to change, from 1 to 5. The default is the active profiles.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/myproX2/prox2_backup_perfis.json
Default backup file. The rate and dpi commands create it when it does not exist, and never overwrite it.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/myproX2/painel_dados/
Data of the web panel.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/60\-prox2.rules
Gives the logged in user access to the receiver hidraw device.
.PP
The data folder follows
.BR XDG_DATA_HOME .
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
prox2 status
prox2 bateria \-\-seguir
prox2 rate 1000
prox2 dpi 1600 \-\-perfil 1 2
prox2 backup perfis.json
prox2 painel \-\-sem\-navegador
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR myprox2 (1)
.SH AUTHOR
jonanthann
